<title>UK: UK Dec non-EU trade deficit 844 mln stg.</title>
<headline>UK Dec non-EU trade deficit 844 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released following seasonally adjusted UK non-EU Trade data-</p>
<p>    UK TRADE NON-EU (in million stg)    DEC	NOV    (PREL DEC)</p>
<p>    Trade balance			-844     -699     (-639)</p>
<p>    Exports (FOB)			5,833    6,008   (6,031)</p>
<p>    Imports (FOB)			6,677    6,707   (6,670)</p>
<p>    Oil exports			    297	263     (263)</p>
<p>    Oil imports			    386	449     (448)</p>
<p>    Trade balance 3m ending	 -1,996	n/a  (-1,862)</p>
<p>NOTE - Consensus forecast 641 million stg deficit.  </p>
<p>TRADE VOLUME EX OIL/ERRATICS</p>
<p>    Import volume index (base 1990) 149.1    147.6   (147.1)</p>
<p>    Export volume index (base 1990) 124.9    137.3   (137.4)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports)  unch     1.0%    (1.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (imps)   9.5%   11.0%   (10.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports)  -1.5%    1.0%    (1.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (exps)   6.0%    8.0%    (8.0%)</p>
<p>TRADE VALUE EX OIL/ERRATICS</p>
<p>    Balance (million stg)		  -1,059    -619     (-569)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports)  -1.0%    0.5%    (0.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports)  -1.5%    1.0%    (1.0%)</p>
<p>The ONS said provisional estimates show both export and import prices virtually unchanged compared with November. Between December 1995 and December 1996 export prices have risen by 0.5 percent while import prices have fallen by 3.5 percent.</p>
</text>
